  "provenance": {
    "commit": "98a8d20f306544f19c572cc72914877165417a5e",
    "subject": "prepare feature-24",
    "why": "The last commit before feature-24 touched the generator. Every result a player has in localStorage today was written against this tree, so this is the only tree that can say what those results were solved on.",
    "how": "git archive 98a8d20 into a temp tree with the repo's node_modules linked in, then resolved each date with THAT tree's own selectGrooveForDate, GROOVES and answerOf. Nothing here was read off the working tree.",
    "taken": "2026-09-05",
    "span": "2026-06-07 to 2026-09-04 — 90 consecutive local days, three full laps of the thirty-groove rotation, so every groove appears at least once and the lap-boundary swap in orderFor is exercised twice.",
    "catalogueLength": 30,
    "doNotRegenerate": "Never regenerate this from the tree that broke it: it would then agree with whatever moved and prove nothing. If one of the four things in docs/music.md § What must never change has moved — src/lib/hash.ts, MUSIC_LABEL and its draw order, the order of FLAVOURS or of a template’s own flavours list, or a groove’s uuid — restore what moved and leave this file alone. The one exception is a catalogue that has grown; see ifTheCatalogueGrows.",
    "ifTheCatalogueGrows": "A thirty-first groove reassigns every past date, because selectGrooveForDate indexes a seeded shuffle of the whole catalogue. That is sanctioned and costs no player anything — nothing in the app ever re-resolves a past date, a stored result carries its own grooveId, and a share link resolves by uuid — and feature-7 R6 settled it: “Days before the change keep whatever they were shown, because DailyResult.grooveId records what was actually played.” So when catalogueLength no longer matches GROOVES.length, re-baseline this record rather than restoring the catalogue. Take the new record from an archive of the tree as it stood BEFORE the growth, never from the tree that grew it: git archive <the last commit before the growth> | tar -x -C <scratch>/pre, symlink the repo’s node_modules into it, then emit the days with npx vitest run --root <scratch>/pre --project app so they resolve through THAT tree’s selectGrooveForDate, GROOVES and answerOf. Regenerating from the tree that made the change would silently bless anything else that moved in it, which is the exact failure this record exists to prevent. Span three full laps of the new size so no groove is left unwatched, and set catalogueLength to the new length."
  },
